title: 'One pacer runs at a time: ''pacer.sh run'' refuses while another pacer lives, or while a session a killed pacer started still runs.'
pid: e3f4f52e-386b-415e-b34f-5a1f19d7f5f2
body: |2-
  Built 2026-11-15 at Top's asking, after two sessions ran at once that
  morning. The refusal is a line in 'pacer.log' and on the output, naming
  the pacer or the session that stopped it; a pid file or a
  'running-session' file whose process is gone stops nothing. The
  script's header ("ONE PACER") says how; 'tools/team/test_pacer.py'
  tries it on a copy in a temporary folder, spending nothing.
contains:
